"""Digit glyph table for Matiks duels.

Matiks draws the question's digits as SVG vector outlines, not text — there
is no "46" anywhere in the DOM, only <path d="M6.62 24.24...">. So the digits
cannot be read the way the rest of the page can.

They are, however, deterministic: one fixed path per digit. This table maps
each path back to its digit, which is exact rather than probabilistic — a
strictly better outcome than OCR-ing the pixels.

Regenerate with tools/build_glyphs.py if Matiks changes its font.
"""

